g&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323870" owner_email="bmahadev@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/70/323870/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iab43619d629885b14792962b0182ba27b182a850" commit="b161b2ab642ee25d0cce393a86efad2f04ed4a53" commit_message="[autotest] Log time used to run autoupdater for CrOS  The stats data will be used to monitor the overall history of time used to run AU and Paygen test.  BUG=chromium:561036 TEST=None  Change-Id: Iab43619d629885b14792962b0182ba27b182a850 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323397 Commit-Ready: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Alex Deymo &lt;deymo@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323397" owner_email="dshi@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/97/323397/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I96c3da2bc14e88bd9df0c77a55dc93197cc515e5" commit="e229bb3a1e10bd920f4d1fa3c5cacda72aebd9c3" commit_message="servo: Add control to dynamically change loglevel.  It'd be nice to change the loglevel of servod without having to restart the process entirely.  This change adds a control, loglevel, which allows the user to query and set the log level without restarting servod.  BUG=chromium:580684 BRANCH=None TEST=cros_workon hdctools for the host.  Emerge hdctools, run servod and use dut-control to query the current log level.  Verify that it is 'info'.  Use dut-control to change the loglevel to debug and verify that the log messages appear with the proper debug formatting.  Use dut-control again to change the loglevel back to info and verify that no debug log messages are emitted.  Change-Id: I96c3da2bc14e88bd9df0c77a55dc93197cc515e5 Signed-off-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323542 Commit-Ready: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323542" owner_email="aaboagye@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/hdctools" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/hdctools" ref="refs/changes/42/323542/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I65e711a5fb168d3c266de03921431df7c186258d" commit="4a9e0fee14bfd301f4112e3e9fc30985f3fb6807" commit_message="Change factory related build logic to use virtual/target-os-factory{-shim}.  The new target-os-factory and target-os-factory-shim packages provide a simpler way to manage factory related packages so we don't need to hard-code and list individual package names any more.  The make_factory_toolkit script is still using explicit package list because it's merging packages without dependency and should be revised in future.  BUG=chromium:577601 TEST=build_packages; build_image factory factory_install CQ-DEPEND=CL:322072  Change-Id: I65e711a5fb168d3c266de03921431df7c186258d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/322042 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="322042" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/crosutils" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/crosutils" ref="refs/changes/42/322042/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2722655c970e771bc88b33cb84a69195e1fac5d6" commit="ae18d6c61477411e63c94f24298cca49a3fcb82e" commit_message="Cyclone Board: Add i2c support in Cyclone  Add i2c support in Cyclone.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47463 TEST=emerge-cyclone depthcharge compiles successfully BRANCH=tot  Change-Id: I2722655c970e771bc88b33cb84a69195e1fac5d6 Signed-off-by: Ruilin Hao &lt;rlhao@marvell.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/314027 Commit-Ready: Kan Yan &lt;kyan@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Kan Yan &lt;kyan@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kan Yan &lt;kyan@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="314027" owner_email="rlhao@marvell.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/27/314027/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic20be2024afedabc2d8bc767f1b794376348523c" commit="8d557702e74438cf1032bf7c0bf97d5df152c63c" commit_message="vb20: add vb2api_check_hash_get_digest() for retrieving hash result  For x86 systems, which resume through the boot reset vector, to implement vboot verification of the memory init code one needs check that the slot chosen on the resume path is the same as the original boot path. That check is done by storing the resulting hash of the slot. However, vb2api doesn't export the resulting hash from vb2api_check_hash(). Thus, provide a variant which saves the resulting digest in the supplied buffer.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46049 BRANCH=glados TEST=Suspended and resumed on chell. Also, tested with an EC build      which returns a bad hash to ensure that is properly caught.  Change-Id: Ic20be2024afedabc2d8bc767f1b794376348523c Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323460 Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323460" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/60/323460/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3c6a3e97a3853b6ed9a46d354520ad75e8442b10" commit="bc58bddc4f11aaa8781aec8b131173d1980a2cea" commit_message="Build dev-util/bsdiff from AOSP.  bsdiff have seen some improvements in AOSP source based on the code we had in Chromium OS plus some extra changes in the AOSP side. More updates will come, so this CL switches the dev-util/bsdiff ebuild to build from AOSP.  List of new CLs included in this build. Not all of them important for Chromium OS.   f822e6c Fix reading extents file if not start from the beginning of a extent.   d87c835 Various fixes in bspatch and File class.   cdbad9a Build bspatch for the target.   cd1e453 Update NOTICE and LICENSE file.   792b0a5 Build unittests on Android.   437b7af bspatch: Re-enable extents support.   b870eb5 bspatch: Ran clang-format on bspatch.cc.   daf3516 FileInterface: Implement GetSize().   03f1deb bspatch: Use a C++ interface for file access.   20891f9 Convert C sources to C++.   e1526cf Ran clang-format on all the Chromium OS sources.   a09afd9 Merge &quot;Disable GNU extensions in bspatch code.&quot;   870b802 Disable GNU extensions in bspatch code.   b7e3b8e Update Android.mk to build Chromium OS changes.  BUG=chromium:580717 TEST=`emerge-link bsdiff` with and without cros_workon enabled.  Change-Id: I3c6a3e97a3853b6ed9a46d354520ad75e8442b10 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323383 Commit-Ready: Alex Deymo &lt;deymo@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Alex Deymo &lt;deymo@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323383" owner_email="deymo@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/83/323383/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If8635837f4b2a9858c280b680d7aeff875788b45" commit="adacf121c3df1332ac75608d96c2f023bf9b3a46" commit_message="Add python script to measure drag latency using QuuickStep V2  minimization.py is a helper module implementing an alternative method for processing the data. It shifts the laser event timestamps in small steps until they sit nicely on on a straight line as they would if latency was zero.  Example plot with XY data and fitted lines for the shifted laser events https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B7f9CeY-0HXFUWwwbVdlLXpMVEE  qstep.py runs evtest as a separate process, talks to QuickStep over serial and saves data from both as files. I then runs both data processing scripts on those files.  Example run:          $ python qstep.py 6         Input device   : /dev/input/event6         Serial device  : /dev/ttyACM1         Laser log file : /tmp/QuickStep_2016_01_21__1554_22_lsaer.log         evtest log file: /tmp/QuickStep_2016_01_21__1554_22_evtest.log         Clock zeroed at 1453409662 (rt 0.259ms)         ........................................         Processing data, may take a minute or two...         Drag latency (min method) = 19.62 ms         Average Maximum Minimum         0.0237723313845 0.0333168506622 0.0167829990387  The ~4 ms difference between the two methods is close to 4.8 ms which is half the typical interval between two consecutive readings in evtest log. We previously verified that similar difference arises depending on whether we look at the last reading before the crossing, first one after, or interpolated crossing time between them.  BUG=none TEST=run manually on Glimmer (Lenovo rugged convertible)  Change-Id: If8635837f4b2a9858c280b680d7aeff875788b45 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323170 Commit-Ready: Mark Koudritsky &lt;kamrik@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mark Koudritsky &lt;kamrik@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mark Koudritsky &lt;kamrik@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323170" owner_email="kamrik@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/touchbot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/touchbot" ref="refs/changes/70/323170/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.8" change_id="I7d0aec0b60afd8506a9136ed62fd647caec748aa" commit="45a49283655ef6008dc9b14f6f8465e3a49ec683" commit_message="CHROMIUM: CONFIG: Enable VGEM on exynos  In an effort to enable VGEM everywhere, I am flipping the switch on kernel 3.8 + exynos.  BUG=none TEST=untested  Change-Id: I7d0aec0b60afd8506a9136ed62fd647caec748aa Signed-off-by: Stphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/314891 Commit-Ready: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="314891" owner_email="marcheu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/91/314891/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie5ada9c5441b5b042bd0801d66559ab715fbbf47" commit="9f20c12eaf94602749ac2db55c2b83a15045acdf" commit_message="Increase MAX_CUSTOM_DELAY to 5 minutes  Rialto will soon need a longer dev mode delay, this variable would prevent it.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:48657 TEST=See follow up CLs BRANCH=master  Change-Id: Ie5ada9c5441b5b042bd0801d66559ab715fbbf47 Signed-off-by: Alexandru M Stan &lt;amst